<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  THE DATE ARITHMETIC AXIS, negative half. THIS FILE IS SUPPOSED TO FAIL.

  Its sibling `clamp.dmn` shows that FEEL's `date + duration("P1Y")` clamps. On
  its own that is only half an argument, because the obvious way to write an
  anniversary is not a duration at all: increment the YEAR and rebuild the date
  from its components. If that worked, the exporter would need no duration
  lowering and `daydate` would need no `add years`.

  It does not work. `date(2025, 2, 29)` is not a date, and both engines answer
  NULL rather than clamping or rolling. So an anniversary written by
  reconstruction has NO correct lowering to give it, and the decision that
  depends on it goes null too, which is the second decision here.

  Worse, the three implementations disagree in three directions, which is why
  the corpus fixes the idiom rather than leaving it to the author:

    L4 `Date 29 2 2025`        -> 2025-03-01   (lenient; ROLLS FORWARD)
    FEEL `date(2025, 2, 29)`   -> null         (both engines, measured)
    FEEL `d + duration("P1Y")` -> 2025-02-28   (both engines, measured)

  The `expect` block therefore asks for the CLAMPED answer, the one the corpus
  actually means, and this file is red precisely because reconstruction cannot
  produce it. A green run here would mean an engine had started accepting an
  impossible date, and the standing advice in `daydate` and in L4.Dmn.Lower
  against reconstructing components would need rechecking.

  Driven as HarnessMustFail, the same construction as `dmn-xsd-order`'s negative
  and `date-axis-badannotation.dmn`: a gate that has only ever been seen green is
  not evidence that it is connected to anything.

  NOT AN EMITTED GOLDEN. Never regenerate.
-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" id="definitions_reconstruct_refused" name="reconstruction refused" namespace="https://legalese.com/l4/dmn/reconstruct_refused">
  <inputData id="in_issued" name="issued">
    <variable id="in_issued_var" name="issued" typeRef="date"/>
  </inputData>
  <decision id="d_anniv_reconstruct" name="anniv_reconstruct">
    <variable id="v_anniv_reconstruct" name="anniv_reconstruct" typeRef="date"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_anniv_reconstruct"><requiredInput href="#in_issued"/></informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="l_anniv_reconstruct">
      <text>date(issued.year + 1, issued.month, issued.day)</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decision id="d_anniv_duration" name="anniv_duration">
    <variable id="v_anniv_duration" name="anniv_duration" typeRef="date"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_anniv_duration"><requiredInput href="#in_issued"/></informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="l_anniv_duration">
      <text>issued + duration("P1Y")</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
</definitions>
